igh-risk populations"},{"text":"Readmission patterns"},{"text":"Treatment adherence challenges"},{"text":"Follow-up gaps"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Psychiatric nurses with basic data literacy will increasingly be able to work effectively within these digital systems."}]},{"heading":"Target Profile at Graduation","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A strong Psychiatric Nurse candidate should ideally demonstrate:"},{"type":"h","text":"Clinical"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Patient assessment"},{"text":"Vital monitoring"},{"text":"Medication administration"},{"text":"Emergency response"},{"text":"Infection prevention"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Psychiatric"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Mental-status examination"},{"text":"Therapeutic communication"},{"text":"Psychiatric nursing care"},{"text":"Behavioral observation"},{"text":"Crisis intervention"},{"text":"Suicide-risk recognition"},{"text":"De-escalation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Rehabilitation"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Psychoeducation"},{"text":"Family support"},{"text":"Recovery-oriented care"},{"text":"Community follow-up"},{"text":"Relapse-prevention support"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Professional"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Confidentiality"},{"text":"Ethics"},{"text":"Patient dignity"},{"text":"Documentation"},{"text":"Team communication"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Digital"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"EMR/EHR"},{"text":"Hospital Information Systems"},{"text":"Excel"},{"text":"Tele-mental-health platforms"},{"text":"Data privacy"}]}]},{"heading":"Recommended Final Skill Stack","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Professional Nursing Foundation"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Psychiatric / Mental Health Nursing"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Mental-Status Examination"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Therapeutic Communication"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Crisis Intervention"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Suicide & Self-Harm Risk Recognition"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Psychiatric Pharmacology"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"De-escalation"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Addiction & Rehabilitation"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Trauma-Informed Care"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Family & Patient Psychoeducation"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Clinical Documentation"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"EMR / Digital Mental Health"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Research & Evidence-Based Practice"}]},{"heading":"Best Overall Positioning","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"flow","items":["Recognized Nursing Qualification","Professional Registration","Strong Clinical Nursing Foundation","Psychiatric/Mental Health Clinical Exposure","Specialized Mental-Health Nursing Education","Psychiatric Nurse","Senior Psychiatric Nurse","Mental-Health Specialist/Coordinator/Educator"]},{"type":"p","text":"For this career, the strongest profile is professional nursing competence + psychiatric assessment + therapeutic communication + crisis management + medication monitoring + suicide-risk recognition + rehabilitation + family education + digital-health skills."},{"type":"note","label":"Career-fitment mapping note","text":"Because the target role is Psychiatric Nurse, this pathway should primarily be mapped to students pursuing a recognized nursing qualification and professional registration. The “Forensic Nursing / Psychiatric Nursing (Post-Basic)” specialization should be treated as a specialization layer rather than assuming that every B.Sc/BPT/BOT/BMLT graduate is independently eligible for psychiatric nursing practice."}]}]}